 ],
 "literal": "Thinking of her, I will see, I am like, her thorn-sharp teeth / and nectar-oozing beautiful red mouth, fragrant eaglewood / and sandalwood smelling, black-sand-like hair, / great, beautiful, cool-eyed mountain girl's / gentle smile with a laugh, and exuberant look.",
 "translation": "Whenever I think of her, I seem to see her right before me: the mountain girl with thorn-sharp teeth, a beautiful red mouth oozing nectar, hair like black river-sand smelling of fragrant eaglewood and sandalwood, and great, beautiful, cool eyes. I see her gentle smile and her exuberant look.",
 "modern": "நினைத்துப் பார்க்கும்போதெல்லாம் அவளை நேரில் காண்பது போல உணர்கிறேன்; முள் போன்ற பற்களையும், அமிழ்தம் சுரக்கும் அழகான சிவந்த வாயையும், அகிலும் சந்தனமும் கமழும் ஆற்று மணல் போன்ற கூந்தலையும், பெரிய குளிர்ந்த கண்களையும் உடைய அந்தக் குறிஞ்சி நிலப் பெண்ணின் புன்னகையையும், அவளது செருக்குமிக்க பார்வையையும் நான் காண்கிறேன்.",
 "explanation": "In this poem, the hero speaks about his beloved, a mountain girl, expressing how deeply she is etched in his mind. He says that whenever he thinks of her, she appears vividly before his eyes as if she were physically present. He describes her sharp, thorn-like teeth, her sweet red mouth that seems to ooze nectar, and her dark hair that smells of fragrant eaglewood and sandalwood, resembling the black sand of a riverbed. Her large, cool eyes and her gentle, proud smile are unforgettable to him. This poem belongs to the Kuriñci (mountainous) landscape, as indicated by the word 'koṭicci' (mountain girl) and the fragrant forest trees like akil and sandalwood.",
